# TASK 03 – CONSTRUCTORS IN DERIVED CLASSES AND MEMBER CLASSES (9 MARKS)

## 3.1 Pass Values to Base Constructors (3 Marks)

Constructors of derived classes pass values to their base classes using member initializer lists.

```cpp
Student(string n, int i, string p, string prog, double c)
    : Person(n, i, p)
{
    program = prog;
    cgpa = c;
}
```

For TeachingAssistant, the most-derived class directly initializes the virtual base class Person.

```cpp
TeachingAssistant(string n, int i, string p,
                 string prog, double c,
                 string d, double s)
    : Person(n, i, p),
      Student(n, i, p, prog, c),
      Staff(n, i, p, d, s)
{
}
```

**Explanation:** In virtual inheritance, the most-derived class is responsible for constructing the virtual base class. Therefore, TeachingAssistant must initialize Person directly.

