## 3.2 Member Classes (2 Marks)

Member classes represent a has-a relationship. A Person has an Address, and a Student has a Course.

```cpp
class Address
{
private:
    string city;
    int pin;

public:
    Address(string c, int p)
    {
        city = c;
        pin = p;
    }
};

class Course
{
private:
    string courseName;
    int courseCode;

public:
    Course(string c, int code)
    {
        courseName = c;
        courseCode = code;
    }
};
```

Address is a member class of Person, and Course is a member class of Student. Their constructors receive values through the constructor of the containing class.

