## 3.3 Trace the Order of Construction and Destruction (3 Marks)

### Program

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

struct Person
{
    Person()
    {
        cout << "Person ";
    }

    ~Person()
    {
        cout << "~Person ";
    }
};

struct Student : virtual Person
{
    Student()
    {
        cout << "Student ";
    }

    ~Student()
    {
        cout << "~Student ";
    }
};

struct Staff : virtual Person
{
    Staff()
    {
        cout << "Staff ";
    }

    ~Staff()
    {
        cout << "~Staff ";
    }
};

struct TeachingAssistant : Student, Staff
{
    TeachingAssistant()
    {
        cout << "TA ";
    }

    ~TeachingAssistant()
    {
        cout << "~TA ";
    }
};

int main()
{
    cout << "Student object: ";
    {
        Student s;
    }

    cout << "\nStaff object: ";
    {
        Staff st;
    }

    cout << "\nTeachingAssistant object: ";
    {
        TeachingAssistant ta;
    }

    cout << endl;
    return 0;
}
```

### Output

```text
Student object: Person Student ~Student ~Person
Staff object: Person Staff ~Staff ~Person
TeachingAssistant object: Person Student Staff TA ~TA ~Staff ~Student ~Person
```

### Explanation

**Construction order:**

1. Virtual base classes are constructed first.
2. Direct base classes are constructed next, in declaration order.
3. Member objects are constructed in declaration order.
4. The derived class constructor executes last.

**Destruction order:**

Destruction happens in the reverse order of construction.

