## 3.4 Experiment – Remove Virtual (1 Mark)

Remove virtual from both Student and Staff.

```cpp
struct Student : Person
{
};

struct Staff : Person
{
};
```

### Expected Change in Output

For a TeachingAssistant object, Person is constructed twice because Student and Staff now contain separate Person subobjects.

```text
Person Student Person Staff TA
```

### Explanation

With virtual inheritance, TeachingAssistant contains only one shared Person subobject.

Without virtual inheritance, it contains two separate Person subobjects.

Therefore:

- Constructor output changes because Person is constructed twice.
- sizeof(TeachingAssistant) may increase because of the extra Person subobject.
- Accessing common Person members can become ambiguous.

To compare object size, use:

```cpp
cout << "Size of TeachingAssistant: "
     << sizeof(TeachingAssistant) << endl;
```

The exact size depends on the compiler and memory padding.

